{
  "claims": [
    {
      "kind": "qualitative",
      "text": "Geopolitical conflicts could reduce net sales, earnings and cash flows, including through economic recessions, inflationary pressures, and energy and supply chain cost increases, weakening cash flow available for debt repayment.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0026",
          "quote": "there could be additional negative impacts to our net sales, earnings and cash flows should these situations worsen or other geopolitical conflicts arise"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "qualitative",
      "text": "Disruptions in credit markets, changes to credit ratings, or disruptions to banking partners may reduce access to credit or overall liquidity, directly impairing the company's ability to refinance debt.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0026",
          "quote": "Disruptions in credit markets or to our banking partners or changes to our credit ratings may reduce our access to credit or overall liquidity."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "qualitative",
      "text": "The company's significant floating-rate and foreign currency debt and derivative positions expose it to interest-rate and foreign exchange movements upon refinancing, which could adversely affect cash flows and interest expense.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0020",
          "quote": "We have a significant amount of debt, including floating rate and foreign currency debt and derivatives, as part of our capital markets activities."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0020",
          "quote": "As we refinance debt or renew derivatives, we are exposed to movement in global interest rates and rate differentials."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0020",
          "quote": "The maturity cash outflows of foreign currency debt and derivative instruments could be adversely impacted by significant appreciation of foreign currency exchange rates"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "qualitative",
      "text": "A slowdown, recession, or inflationary pressures could reduce product demand and cause customers or other business partners financial hardship, reducing sales, income, and cash flow available for debt repayment.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0021",
          "quote": "Uncertain economic or social conditions may adversely impact demand for our products or cause our customers and other business partners to suffer financial hardship, which could adversely impact our business."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0022",
          "quote": "A slow-down, recession or inflationary pressures in the general economy; reduced market growth rates; tighter credit markets for our suppliers, vendors or customers"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "kind": "quantitative",
      "text": "The scorecard's strongest factor is EBITDA / interest at {{m:interest_coverage:LTM}} (band {{m:band_interest_coverage:latest}}, weight {{m:weight_interest_coverage:latest}}); debt / EBITDA at {{m:debt_to_ebitda:LTM}} (band {{m:band_debt_to_ebitda:latest}}, weight {{m:weight_debt_to_ebitda:latest}}), net leverage at {{m:net_leverage:LTM}} (band {{m:band_net_leverage:latest}}, weight {{m:weight_net_leverage:latest}}) and FCF / debt at {{m:fcf_to_debt:LTM}} (band {{m:band_fcf_to_debt:latest}}, weight {{m:weight_fcf_to_debt:latest}}) also score well, while liquidity coverage at {{m:liquidity_coverage:LTM}} (band {{m:band_liquidity_coverage:latest}}, weight {{m:weight_liquidity_coverage:latest}}) and near-term maturity cover at {{m:near_term_maturity_cover:FY0}} (band {{m:band_near_term_maturity_cover:latest}}, weight {{m:weight_near_term_maturity_cover:latest}}) are the weakest.",
      "citations": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "quantitative",
      "text": "The {{m:sb_grade:latest}} grade is a stylized internal scorecard grade, not a credit rating, and it is not provisional because all six scorecard factors were scored, producing a weighted score of {{m:sb_score:latest}}.",
      "citations": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "qualitative",
      "text": "Earlier findings that P&G is a global market leader in fabric care, baby care and feminine care support the strong business risk profile underlying the scorecard result.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0079",
          "quote": "In fabric care, we generally have the number one or number two market share position and are the global market leader with over 35% market share"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0079",
          "quote": "In baby care, we are a global market leader"
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0079",
          "quote": "We are the global market leader in the feminine care category with nearly 30% global market share."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "qualitative",
      "text": "The weak liquidity coverage and near-term maturity cover scores are partially offset by management's expectation that short-term liquidity and operating needs can be supported largely through cash generated from operations and by currently undrawn bank credit facilities expected to remain undrawn.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0116",
          "quote": "We anticipate being able to support our short-term liquidity and operating needs largely through cash generated from operations."
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "PG-000008042426000103-0117",
          "quote": "These facilities are currently undrawn and we anticipate that they will remain undrawn."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "qualitative",
      "text": "The scorecard outcome is tempered by earlier downside risk findings, including geopolitical conflicts and credit market disruptions that could weaken cash flow or refinancing access.",
